## US-003 done

**Changes**
- `backend/src/mailer/mailer.js` — the two `console.log` in `transporter.verify` are now `strapi.log.error` (SMTP failure) and `strapi.log.info` (server ready).
- `backend/src/admin/app.example.js` — removed `console.log(app)` from the example `bootstrap`. This is admin-panel (browser) code where `strapi.log` doesn't exist, so it's left as an empty body with a comment.
- Deleted `backend/src/api/document/content-types/document/lifecycles.js` and `backend/src/api/project/content-types/project/lifecycles.js` — both files were wrapped entirely in `/* ... */` (23 of the 27 `console.*` lived there), so there was no active code to migrate. Neighboring HTML templates left untouched.
- `backend/scripts/seed-test-users.js` untouched (CLI script).

**Verification**
- `grep -rn 'console\.' backend/src` → no output.
- `backend/package.json` unchanged (no `@strapi/*` version touched).
- `cd backend && npm test` → 90/90 tests pass. Note: with the machine's default Node 26 the suite fails before running anything (`buffer-equal-constant-time` uses `SlowBuffer`, removed in Node ≥24); the package's `engines` pins `node <=20`, so I ran it with nvm's Node 20.20.2. The test output also shows the SMTP verify error flowing through `strapi.log.error`, confirming the global is available in that callback.

**Progress notes** appended to `.ralph-tui/progress.md`, plus two new patterns at the top (backend logging rules, and the Node 20 requirement for backend tests).

